# Gorilla 158 port fix
# Search-config-v2.json was not valid JSON: the 07.TOOLKIT hunk empties specificDefaults (no per-region or partner default engine) by removing 157's array, and 158's array is longer, so a 32-line tail of it was left after the new []. The tail is removed; the file parses and specificDefaults is [] as the patch intends. lesson: a hunk that replaces a whole JSON value must be ported by value (parse, replace the key, write), never by line count; and every changed .json must parse at the step, not first at final-checks
